  -- NO BALANCE RELIEF, deliberately. It used to cut the balance's whole 5.30
  -- SWEEP out of this plate, but the swing sits at 3.34 and this plate's
  -- underside is at 3.85, so the wheel was never the thing to clear. What it has
  -- to clear is the balance BRIDGE, which reaches 3.89 -- and the 232 rotation
  -- above is chosen so the plate's own notch does that in plan, to 0.1%. Cutting
  -- the sweep as well took more than half the plate away.
  -- The centre used to be a 2.44 bore with a pocket for the rotor's ring. Both
  -- are gone: under the post architecture the bearing lands in a counterbore
  -- cut at the bottom of this part, and 31-3's ring runs below the roof.
  -- The six openings page 6 draws through the plate.
